Description:
The Institute for Earth Education is a not-for-profit, volunteer organisation made up of an international network of individuals and member organisations. We believe that a special kind of education - EARTH EDUCATION - can make a significant difference in the health of our planet.

The Institute...
    * Develops and disseminates Earth Education programmes and activities;
    * Conducts workshops for teachers, leaders and others involved in educating people about environmental problems;
    * Has a range of books and programme materials available from the mail order catalogue;
    * Publishes various journals and newsletter;
    * Supports a network of Major and local Branches.

Our major work is to design and develop specific educational programmes that change people's view of our home, the planet earth, and the way we interact with it.

Raw AD Limited is a company with company registration number 07789355 registered in the United Kingdom in 2011.  Raw AD is in a joint adventure with Clean Gen.  Together the two companies are focusing on the developing, constructions and the operating of Anaerobic Digester's (AD) plants in the UK.  Raw AD is responsible for setting up and concluding all the commercial aspects, organizing the financing and finalization of the contracts with third parties (including the EPC contractor). , whereas Mark Felshaw, on behalf of Clean Gen, is responsible for the development of the technical concept of the project, the organizing of the substrates and the operation of the plant. He is also in direct contact with the planners to provide all the information necessary for the permitting phase.  The joint venture is offering to potential project developers the possibility to integrate in their projects a unique patented technology which has been developed by an Italian technology provider, Austep, enabling the project developer to use 100% of chicken manure in projects (instead of up to 30%). RawAD's vision is to:

--    Help farmers to turn the problem of bio-waste like animal slurry into a regular income stream that increases every year from the sale of electricity and organic fertiliser the ADs generate;
--    Create a low-risk investment opportunity that yields a guaranteed annual return of at least 10% per annum for investors;
--    Offer a profitable business opportunity to our partners and Raw AD itself;
--    Create a highly desirable solution that reduces greenhouse gas emissions and creates wealth for society as a whole.

Our aim is to offer a unique ‘one-stop shop’ where customers can choose from a combination of energy saving measures at low inconvenience and at low or no financial cost. We work with various Government initiatives promoting energy saving products to achieve our goal: That every home has access to the most up-to-date energy efficient technology on the market. Going forward, our goal is to expand our product list to include many more energy efficient measures and to offer our customers the best energy solutions in the industry.

To that end we will continue to be fair, honest, transparent, appropriate and professional in our dealings with all our customers. Any information we give, will be:

- Complete, accurate and truthful, both in terms of what we say and what we don’t say;
- In plain and easy to understand language;
- Related to products and services appropriate for the customer.

Vulcain Engineering Ltd is an ambitious engineering consultancy which is supporting the UK Government’s policy objective of 2050 Net Zero Carbon through its involvement in large-scale energy and infrastructure projects. These include: 
-  Hinkley Point C, the largest industrial European construction project; 
-  Various renewable projects; and;
-  Fusion research. 

We want to be part of the on-going changes and transformation of infrastructure and energy production to meet the challenges of climate change. This involvement provides focus and meaning to our day-to-day work.

Vulcain Engineering Ltd is the UK subsidiary of Vulcain Engineering Group, an international company which operates in 40 countries and employs over 2700 staff worldwide. We are proud that synergy with the group offers us a strong skill-set and corporate reach-back that enables us to perform in small regional as well as massive international projects. While benefiting from being part of the group, Vulcain Engineering also remains a medium-sized company which allows us to retain a flexible and friendly working environment.

asunim specializes in the field of photovoltaic (PV) solar energy and includes several companies in different countries and markets. More than 20 years of experience in solar energy.

Initiated formally in 2005, today asunim develops the following activities:

• Engineering, Procurement and Construction (EPC);
• Project development and Consultancy;
• Tailor made photovoltaic self-consumption solutions with grid injection or zero injection; 100% self-consumption and self-consumption with battery storage;
• Wholesale of solar modules, inverters, batteries, charge controllers, solar pumping systems and all other required PV system components worldwide.

asunim designs solutions for on- and off-grid solar power systems of all sizes and provides its clients with a safe bet for their future energy requirements. asunim covers the supply chain with high-quality components cautiously selected using knowledge gained from many years of experience, and supports its customers with professional logistics services, specialized training sessions, and technical support provided by our multilingual team.

Our long-term associated equipment manufacturers, have a current total volume of 850MW supplied or installed via asunim and are the best in their field regarding quality workmanship, superior design, competitive pricing, on-time delivery, after-sales support, and continuous product innovation.

Communities for Renewables CIC (CfR) helps local energy enterprises to develop, finance and manage their own renewable energy generation. CfR also provides strategic advice to help develop and implement a wide range of local energy business models that help reduce and localise energy spend, tackle fuel poverty, and earn income to re-invest in the local community.

Since setting up in 2012, CfR has worked with over 20 local energy enterprises, local authorities and social landlords across the UK. Over the last 2 years CfR has helped to develop and finance nearly £30 million of community-owned solar projects ranging from solar PV panels on community buildings to one of the largest community-owned solar farms in the UK. CfR’s role in delivering these projects has included supporting:

•	Local energy enterprise set-up (including company formation, governance set-up, policies, director mentoring and admin set-up);
•	Business planning and exploring new business models, including smart energy technologies and local supply;
•	Community and stakeholder engagement strategies;
•	Site searching including technical and financial feasibility assessments;
•	Project development (including planning, landowner/host engagement and legal agreements, grid connection and procurement);
•	Managing the community purchase of renewable energy projects from commercial developers (including management of legal and financial advisors but not providing legal and financial advice);
•	Finance transaction management and support for construction and long-term finance from commercial lenders, social investors and community share / bond offers (including management of legal and financial advisors but not providing legal and financial advice);
•	Ongoing company admin and asset management.

We do two things;

Capital Green Talent (www.capitalgreen.eu) is a global search, selection & recruitment consultancy that specialises in sourcing the world's highest achievers across the clean technology (start-ups, early-stage & fast-growth), renewable energy,  private equity, climate change, carbon and environmental sectors. 

Capital Green Connector (http://bit.ly/CG_connector) actively connects renewable energy & clean tech executives, entrepreneurs and companies with potential clients, partners and investors.

The Carbon Catalysts Group is a renewables project development and consulting organisation formed from a network of partners and associates.  

Each member of the organisation brings to the table a significant level of energy industry expertise, providing a substantial knowledge bank and a very wide range of project skills and resources.  Our partners and associates don’t just know the theory – they have hands-on, successful experience in the energy industry.

Carbon Catalysts:
- Offer consultancy and management services; 
- Develop and partner on projects;
- Work with developers, entrepreneurs, lenders and buyers; 
- Provide project leadership and direction;
- Connect opportunities and investors;
- Assist innovators of new technologies;
- Create access routes to the market for “industry outsiders”.

In generation and connection projects we provide support at all levels to any party involved in energy projects from conception and  development through to successful implementation or sale.  Whilst our main focus is on renewable technologies, we have experience of all technologies, including nuclear.

The breadth of experience in our network means we can supply expertise into most projects or problems.
Commercial, regulatory and legal projects are our speciality.

We can offer advice on market entry to take advantage of Government schemes on funding and obligations such as ROCS, FITS, ECO and Green Deal.

If the question has an answer – we will know how to find it!

EcoGenR8 Limited is a development company specialising in cleantech innovation. Our core skills lie in the development of cleantech technologies for which we offer a range of services, from expert consultancy through to the development and delivery of all stages of the innovation cycle from concept through to operations. 

We provide a range of services including:
(i) Specialist consultancy services from technical and commercial due diligence to discreet project work;
(ii) Strategic services such as project origination, feasibility and development;
(iii) Product and technology development and commercialisation;
(iv) Asset optimisation and management;
(v) Engineering services including detailed design, installation and commissioning.  

We offer flexible business models, ranging from discreet consultancy assignments to partnering with technology provider and project developers to share the risk associated with developing technologies and projects.

EGS Energy is leading the development of deep geothermal energy resources in the UK on a commercial scale through its unique access to engineered geothermal system technology and know-how. 


The electricity and heat produced by EGS Energy will be:

large scale; 
sustainable; 
peak load available (95%); 
virtually emissions free; 
from a sustainable resource; and 
small in terms of its physical and environmental footprint.

GreenACT will enable you to capture this low-cost energy to provide electricity and heat for your home.

    We’ll give you an informed view on which technology, or combination of technologies, is right for your home;
    We’ll ensure that you have the right equipment, correctly installed for optimum efficiency and maximum output;
    And we’ll show you how to make the most of the grants and incentives offered by the Government.

For Solar PV Panels, renewable heating systems – including heat pumps and solar hot water – talk to GreenACT, the experts in green energy installation.

Care GREEN is a company with a team of dedicated and qualified professionals continually pursuing the successful implementation of Renewable Energy projects and other energy efficiency measures including energy efficient lighting installations and energy efficient refrigeration units for retail outlets. 
Solar related electrical energy supply.
